2:T74d,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does a kitchen renovation cost in the UK?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"As a rough guide, a cosmetic refresh may cost around £5,000–£10,000, a complete mid-range replacement £12,000–£24,000, and a layout-changing project £18,000–£38,000 or more. Every project differs, so request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it cheaper to renovate a kitchen or replace it?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Keeping sound cabinets and the existing layout is usually cheaper than a full replacement. However, damaged units, poor storage or unsuitable plumbing may make replacement better value over time."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does moving a kitchen sink or cooker add?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The cost depends on access, distances and the condition of the building. As a rough planning guide, moving a service may add around £500–£2,000, but every project differs and a site assessment is needed for a reliable figure. Request a free, no-obligation quote for accurate pricing."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do kitchen renovation quotes include appliances?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not always. Some quotes include named appliances, while others provide an allowance or cover connection only. Check the model, delivery, installation, disposal and VAT before comparing totals."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How can I reduce the cost of a kitchen renovation?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Retain the layout, choose standard cabinet sizes, compare worktop materials, limit structural changes and make the specification clear before ordering. Avoid cutting costs on essential electrical, plumbing and ventilation work."}}]}7:["slug","kitchen-renovation-before-and-after-cost","d"]
